<title>UK: UK Camelot face big bill over 49's case.</title>
<headline>UK Camelot face big bill over 49's case.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK national lottery operator Camelot Group Plc must pay 305,000 stg in costs incurred by UK bookmakers in a case over the 49's numbers game, a spokesman for 49's said on Monday.</p>
<p>Camelot's legal bill for the case, including its own costs, could top 600,000 stg. Camelot would not comment on the total but said it would be paid out of its profits and not from sums earmarked for good causes.</p>
<p>Magistrate Ronald Bartle dismissed Camelot's attempts to have the 49's game declared illegal and awarded costs to the bookmakers. 49's is run by Ladbrokes, Coral and William Hill.</p>
<p>-- Keith Weir, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8793</p>
</text>
